        text: 'A person entitled to the possession of specific immovable property may recover it in the manner provided by the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908. [Note: this is the basis for a suit for possession founded on title — the plaintiff must prove a better title than the defendant, unlike the summary, possession-based remedy under section 6 below. There is no limit on how long ago the plaintiff was dispossessed, unlike section 6\'s strict six-month window, but a title suit takes longer to try since title itself is in issue.]',
