        sectionNo: '27',
        heading: 'Jurisdiction',
        text: '(1) The Court of Judicial Magistrate of the first class or the Metropolitan Magistrate, as the case may be, within the local limits of which— (a) the person aggrieved permanently or temporarily resides or carries on business or is employed; or (b) the respondent resides or carries on business or is employed; or (c) the cause of action has arisen, shall be the competent Court to grant a protection order and other orders under this Act and to try offences under this Act. (2) Any order made under this Act shall be enforceable throughout India. [Note: applications under this Act are, in practice, filed before and heard by a Family Court where one has been constituted for the area under the Family Courts Act, 1984, and by a Judicial Magistrate of the First Class or Metropolitan Magistrate otherwise.]',
